ring_length = GET(cc, 1+2*LINK_SIZE) - (1+4*LINK_SIZE) - 2` where `GET` yields `unsigned int`, so the subtraction wraps in 32 bits before widening to `size_t`. I reproduced that exactly with `GET!(...).wrapping_sub(9).wrapping_sub(2) as usize` rather than \"fixing\" it to 64-bit arithmetic.\n\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ZHr7ad/translation/src/jit.rs` (from `pcre2_jit_compile.c`, non-JIT parts only)\nI confirmed that `pcre2_jit_match_inc.h` and `pcre2_jit_misc_inc.h` are `#include`d unconditionally at the end of the file (outside any `#ifdef SUPPORT_JIT`), so their `#ifndef SUPPORT_JIT` branches are what actually compile.\n- `pcre2_jit_compile_8`: keeps the full non-JIT control flow — `PCRE2_JIT_TEST_ALLOC` handling (`PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_BADOPTION` if other bits set, else `PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_UNSUPPORTED`), `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` on null code, `PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_BADOPTION` for bits outside `PUBLIC_JIT_COMPILE_OPTIONS`, the deprecated `PCRE2_JIT_INVALID_UTF` → sets `re->overall_options |= PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` (this side effect happens even without JIT), then unconditionally returns `PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_BADOPTION`.\n- `pcre2_jit_match_8`: sets and returns `match_data->rc = PCRE2_ERROR_JIT_BADOPTION`.\n- `_pcre2_jit_get_target_8`: returns `\"JIT is not supported\"`. `_pcre2_jit_get_size_8`: 0. `pcre2_jit_stack_create_8`: NULL. `pcre2_jit_free_unused_memory_8`, `pcre2_jit_stack_assign_8`, `pcre2_jit_stack_free_8`, `_pcre2_jit_free_8`, `_pcre2_jit_free_rodata_8`: no-ops.\n\nAll exported names and signatures are unchanged from the stubs, and nothing in `c_src/` was touched.\n\nresult: Translated pcre2_pattern_info.c into translation/src/pattern_info.rs (pcre2_pattern_info_8, pcre2_callout_enumerate_8) and the non-JIT stubs of pcre2_jit_compile.c into translation/src/jit.rs (10 functions); `cargo build --release` compiles the whole crate with no errors or warnings from either file."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens