C case #defines), `Lstart_eptr`/`Lstart_group` ->\n   `(*F).fields.op_brapos.*`, `Lstart_branch` -> `(*F).fields.op_recurse.start_branch` or\n   `(*F).fields.op_cond.start_branch`, `Lsaved_eptr`/`Lsaved_end_subject`/`Ltrue_end_extra`/\n   `Lsaved_moptions` -> `(*F).fields.op_assert_scs.*`, `Lmin`/`Lmax` ->\n   `(*F).fields.op_vreverse.*`. Check crate::types (hf_* structs) for exact names.\n * CHECK_PARTIAL!(), SCHECK_PARTIAL!(), IS_NEWLINE!(p), WAS_NEWLINE!(p) exist.\n * Available locals: F, N, P, frames_top, assert_accept_frame, frame_copy_size, branch_end,\n   branch_start, bracode, offset, length, rrc, proptype, i, fc, number, reptype,\n   group_frame_type, condition, cur_is_word, prev_is_word, utf, ucp, start_ecode,\n   frame_size, top_bracket, match_data, mb.\n * Helpers in crate::matcher: do_callout, match_ref, recurse_update_offsets (another agent\n   is writing them in parallel; unresolved-name errors for them are expected - report).\n   Also crate::tables::_pcre2_OP_lengths_8, crate::script_run::_pcre2_script_run_8,\n   crate::find_bracket::_pcre2_find_bracket_8, crate::string_utils::*, crate::ucd::*,\n   UCD macros, crate::consts::*, and rep_min/rep_max/rep_typ, GF_*, MATCH_*,\n   RECURSE_UNSET from the skeleton (same module).\n\nBUILD/VERIFY LOOP:\n  cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ZHr7ad\n  python3 _gen/assemble_match.py\n  cd translation && cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"error\" -A6 | head -60\nNever edit translation/src/match_engine.rs (generated) or _gen/frag_match_A.rs /\n_gen/frag_match_B.rs (other agents own them).\n\nWork through your range in sequential pieces, re-reading the C source each time.\nDo not modify anything in c_src/.\n\nReport: the C line range covered, the arms/states produced, synthetic states and extra\nlocals declared, cross-module calls, and the build status.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-xpOsEx/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-ZHr7ad