{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"aec82d148bdc53ee8","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_014xwdS7F4CPPQMAC9UXVKbc","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-xpOsEx/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-ZHr7ad/6b19aa16-17c8-42f3-a300-59c20a915dbc/tasks/aec82d148bdc53ee8.output","summary":"I completed a full top-to-bottom walk of `parse_regex` (C lines 3112–5946) against `compile_parse.rs`, in chunks, plus mechanical cross-checks (error-code multisets, `goto`-target counts, `*parsed_pattern++`/`PARSED_LITERAL`/`PUTOFFSET` counts, pointer-arithmetic sites, switch-case label inventories). I also confirmed the crate builds cleanly (`cargo build` → 1 unrelated warning in `dfa_internal.rs`), which validates the type/width choices.\n\n## Result\n\n**No discrepancies found in lines 3112..5946.**\n\n### Chunk-by-chunk verdict\n\n| C lines | Rust | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3112–3226 (decls, MATCH_LINE/WORD prologue, PCRE2_LITERAL path, `end_nests` rounding) | 246–366 | faithful |\n| 3226–3320 (loop-top checks, `inescq` copy) | 366–445 | faithful |\n| 3321–3419 (verb-name processing) | 447–548 | faithful |\n| 3420–3506 (`\\Q`/`\\E`, /x whitespace + `#` comments, `(?#`, quantifier/callout pre-check) | 550–653 | faithful |\n| 3507–3583 (`expect_cond_assert` validation, prev-quantifier modifier patch) | 655–734 | faithful |\n| 3584–3794 (`switch(c)`, `\\` escapes, `ESCAPE_FAILED`, `\\g`/`\\k`) | 742–765, 2205–2455 | faithful |\n| 3795–3886 (`^ $ .`, `* + ?`, `{n,m}`, `CHECK_QUANTIFIER`) | 768–825, 2463–2493 | faithful |\n| 3887–3971 (`[[:<:]]`, top-level POSIX reject, `FROM_PERL_EXTENDED_CLASS` init) | 828–905, 2501–2515 | faithful |\n| 3972–4271 (class loop: `\\Q..\\E`, POSIX names, nested-class start) | 2517–2930 | faithful |\n| 4272–4456 (class end, Perl binary/unary ops, UTS#18 ops) | 2932–3154 | faithful |\n| 4457–4712 (class escapes, `CLASS_LITERAL`, `CLASS_CONTINUE`) | 3156–3508 | faithful |\n| 4713–4876 (`(`, capture, alpha assertions, script runs) | 909–1128 | faithful |\n| 4879–4974 (`(*VERB)` / `(*VERB:NAME)`) | 1130–1263 | faithful |\n| 4977–5170 (`(?` default: `(?\\|`, option set/unset) | 1880–2139 | faithful |\n| 5175–5283 (`(?P…`, `(?R`, `(?+n`, digits, `(?&`, SET_RECURSION/READ_RECURSION_ARGUMENTS) | 1275–1376, 3512–3602 | faithful |\n| 5285–5406 (`(?C` callouts, string & numeric) | 1379–1528 | faithful |\n| 5409–5594 (conditional groups, VERSION, named conditions) | 1531–1794 | faithful |\n| 5597–5677 (atomic group, lookaheads, lookbehinds, POST_ASSERTION) | 1797–1878, 3605–3668 | faithful |\n| 5680–5811 (`DEFINE_NAME`, dup-name scan, list growth, `(?[`) | 1859–1878, 3671–3823 | faithful |\n| 5816–5867 (`\\|`, `)`) | 2147–2202 | faithful |\n| 5871–5946 (PARSED_END, UNCLOSED_PARENTHESIS, FAILED/FAILED_BACK/FAILED_FORWARD) | 3835–3909 | faithful |\n\n### Non-obvious C behaviours that are correctly reproduced (worth noting because they look like bugs)\n\n1. **C 4698–4707** (`CLASS_CONTINUE` end-of-pattern): the `ERR14` assignment is a *separate* `if` (not `else if`) and is therefore always overwritten by the following `if/else` (`ERR112`/`ERR6`), so `ERR14` is dead there. Rust 3479–3495 reproduces this exact structure rather than \"fixing\" it. Correct for literal fidelity.\n2. **C 3939** `errorcode = (*ptr-- == CHAR_COLON)? ERR12 : ERR13;` — the `ptr--` side effect is immediately clobbered by `ptr = tempptr + 2`. Rust 883–892 keeps the (dead) decrement.\n3. **C 5486** `if (*ptr != CHAR_EQUALS_SIGN || (ptr++, !IS_DIGIT(*ptr)))` — the `ptr++` must only happen when the first test is false. Rust 1610–1613 uses a block inside `||`, preserving short-circuit.\n4. **C 4749** `(c = ptr[1])` is only evaluated when `ptrend - ptr > 1`, and the assigned `c` is then consumed by the following `else if (CHMAX_255(c) …)`. Rust 945–955 preserves both the conditional assignment and the later use.\n5. **C 5765 `break;` / 5799 `break;`** inside `DEFINE_NAME` exit the inner `(?` switch, which then hits C 5813 `break` for the outer switch — i.e. a double exit. Rust's `break 'isw` (3772, 3822) is the correct single equivalent.\n6. **`FAILED_BACK`/`FAILED_FORWARD`** (1 and 7 call sites respectively in C) — every Rust `fail_mode = 1/2` is immediately followed by `break 'failed`, so no stale `fail_mode` can leak into an unrelated failure path.\n7. **8-bit macro specialisation**: `MAX_255(c) → 1` (C: `TRUE`) and `CHMAX_255(c) → c <= 255` match the `PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH == 8` + `SUPPORT_UNICODE` configuration; the three dead `META_BIGVALUE` writes (C 3305, 3354, 3396) are correctly absent, and `*parsed_pattern++` counts line up exactly (92 in C − 3 dead = 89 = Rust `PUTPP!` count).\n8. **`PARSED_LITERAL` is a brace-less multi-statement macro** in the 8-bit build (`*p++ = c; okquantifier = TRUE;`). I checked every one of the 10 live call sites: all are in statement position inside braces, so the `okquantifier = TRUE` is never accidentally hoisted out of an `if`. The Rust 3-argument macro is therefore equivalent at every site.\n\n### Cross-check totals (all exact matches)\n- Error codes: every one of the 82 live `errorcode =` assignments matches by value and count (`ERR63`×3, `ERR50`×5, `ERR113`×5, `ERR14`×4, `ERR84`×3, `ERR60`×3, `ERR79`×3, `ERR28`×3, …), including the two conditional forms (`ESC_g?ERR57:ERR69`, `*ptr--==':'?ERR12:ERR13`). The 5 `#ifdef`-dead ones (`ERR85`, `ERR45`×3, `ERR96`) are correctly absent.\n- `goto UNCLOSED_PARENTHESIS`: 9 / 9; `goto FAILED_FORWARD`: 7 / 7; `goto FAILED_BACK`: 1 / 1.\n- `PUTOFFSET`: 9 / 9; `PARSED_LITERAL`: 10 / 10; `nest_depth++`: 7 / 7; `nest_depth--`: 2 / 2; `okquantifier = TRUE`: 12 / 12; `= FALSE`: 2 / 2 (plus decl).\n- `class_range_state` assignments: 14 / 14 in identical order; `class_op_state`: 12 / 12; `class_mode_state`/`new_class_mode_state`: 6 / 6.\n- Pointer arithmetic: `ptrend - ptr` 11 / 11 (all with matching operators `>= 2/3/6/10`, `> 1`, `<= 1`), `tempptr + 2` 5 / 5, `ptr - cb->start_pattern` 7 / 7 (including both `-2` variants at C 5460 → Rust 1575 and C 5648 → Rust 3640), `parsed_pattern[-3]/[-1]` quantifier patch, `parsed_pattern[-2]`/`[-1]` range checks, `previous_callout == parsed_pattern - 4`.\n- Switch inventories: outer `switch(c)` 13/13 labels; inner `switch(*ptr)` after `(?` 15/15 labels; `switch(escape)` (main) 19 explicit + default 19+1; `switch(escape)` (class) with the `default:` → `ESC_A/Z/z/G/K/C` fall-through correctly folded into a single `_ => ERR7`; `switch(meta)` for alpha assertions 7/7 groups.\n- Supporting tables/constants verified: `nest_save` field order and types, `MAX_GROUP_NUMBER=65535`, `MAX_MARK=255`, `ECLASS_NEST_LIMIT=15` (so `>= 14`), `MAX_NAME_COUNT=10000`, `IMM2_SIZE=2`, `NAMED_GROUP_HASH_MASK=0x7fff`, `NAMED_GROUP_IS_DUPNAME=0x8000`, `PUTOFFSET` 2-element (64-bit) variant, `verbs[9]`/`verbcount=9`, `alasmeta[19]`/`alascount=19` with all 19 `len`/`meta` pairs matching, `META_ATOMIC_SCRIPT_RUN=0x8fff0000`.\n\nRelevant files:\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ZHr7ad/c_src/src/pcre2_compile.c`\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ZHr7ad/translation/src/compile_parse.rs`\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ZHr7ad/translation/src/macros.rs` (`PUTOFFSET!`, `GETCHARINCTEST!`, `FORWARDCHARTEST!`, `BACKCHAR!`, `MAX_255!`, `CHMAX_255!`, `is_newline_block`)\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-ZHr7ad/translation/src/compile_tables.rs` (`verbs`, `alasmeta`, `verbnames`, `alasnames`)","usage":{"total_tokens":194137,"tool_uses":41,"duration_ms":585535},"uuid":"a21a0fa7-25a7-40c3-a654-50b3cca34b93","session_id":"6b19aa16-17c8-42f3-a300-59c20a915dbc"}
